---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PhoneCTA from '../../components/PhoneCTA.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import SchemaMarkup from '../../components/SchemaMarkup.astro';
import { config } from '../../config';

const title = 'Nanaimo to Port Alberni Courier | West Coast Delivery';
const description = 'Same-day courier from Nanaimo to Port Alberni. 1.5 hour delivery. Lumber, forestry, industrial parts.';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <SchemaMarkup type="Service" data={{ serviceName: 'Nanaimo to Port Alberni Route', description }} />

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-navy to-brand-blue text-white py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="section-container">
      <h1 class="text-white mb-4">Nanaimo to Port Alberni Courier</h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl opacity-95 mb-8 max-w-2xl">
        Same-day delivery to Port Alberni and West Coast. Forest products, industrial parts, lumber, forestry equipment. 1.5-hour turn-around.
      </p>
      <PhoneCTA text="Get Quote" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Nanaimo ↔ Port Alberni Route</h2>

    <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded mb-8">
      <h3 class="font-bold mb-4 text-brand-blue">Route Overview</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm">
        <li><strong>Distance:</strong> ~80 km via Highway 4 West (Nanaimo Lakes Road)</li>
        <li><strong>Drive time:</strong> 1 hour 15 minutes direct</li>
        <li><strong>Total typical:</strong> 1.5–2 hours door-to-door</li>
        <li><strong>Road condition:</strong> Highway 4 is well-maintained year-round. Mountain passes, winter caution advised.</li>
        <li><strong>Cost:</strong> $35 base + $2.00/km = ~$195 typical</li>
        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Industrial parts, forestry products, lumber</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 section-container">
    <h2>Same-Day Cutoff: Port Alberni</h2>

    <div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Port Alberni</h3>
        <p class="text-lg text-brand-blue font-semibold">1:00 PM cutoff (weekdays)</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-1">Order by 1 PM, delivery by 2:30–3 PM. Mountain route adds 15 minutes vs highway.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Winter Conditions</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Highway 4 mountain passes can be slow in snow. We monitor road reports. Winter same-day is still possible, but order earlier (by 11 AM) to be safe.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Port Alberni Industries We Serve</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Forestry & Lumber Mills</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">Equipment parts, urgent forestry supplies, mill-to-market documentation.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Pulp & Paper Industry</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">Same-day parts delivery for production continuity. Rush service available.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Manufacturing & Fabrication</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">Industrial parts, equipment, finished goods delivery to Port Alberni customers.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Marine Services</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">Port-related document delivery, maritime equipment, urgent cargo handling.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Common Nanaimo ↔ Port Alberni Scenarios</h2>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-blue bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Forestry Equipment Parts</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Mill equipment breaks down; parts needed same-day. Nanaimo supplier ships by 11 AM, delivery by 1 PM in Port Alberni. Downtime costs more than courier. Cost: ~$195 + freight surcharge if oversized.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-blue bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Pulp & Paper Production</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Production line needs urgent supplies. We handle multi-pallet loads (box truck option). Mountain route (Highway 4) adds 15 minutes in winter. Rush available. Cost: $50 base + $2.50/km + weight surcharge.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-blue bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Marine/Port Services</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Port Alberni harbor: shipping documents, marine equipment, urgent cargo. Same-day delivery to port facilities. Cost: ~$195 standard, ~$250+ for oversized freight.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-blue bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Manufacturing Parts Return</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Defective parts back to Nanaimo supplier for replacement. Order by noon, pickup by 12:30 PM, Nanaimo delivery by 2 PM. Cost: ~$195 standard or $250+ if oversized.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 section-container">
    <h2>Winter Route Considerations: Highway 4 Mountain Pass</h2>

    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Port Alberni is accessed via Highway 4 West (Nanaimo Lakes Road). Mountain terrain requires winter planning:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Normal Conditions (Spring–Fall)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Highway 4 is well-maintained year-round. 1 hour 15 min drive time. No surprises. Deliver by 2:30–3 PM if order by 1 PM cutoff.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Winter/Snow (Nov–March)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Mountain passes can be slow. We monitor road reports. If snow, add 20–30 minutes to transit time. Order EARLIER (by 11 AM instead of 1 PM) for same-day winter guarantee. We have chains & experience; drivers prioritized for this route.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Rare Closure</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Highway 4 rarely closes. If it does, we notify you immediately and either delay/reschedule or quote alternative (longer Alberni Inlet route or next-day). You won't be left guessing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Port Alberni Pricing & Cost Examples</h2>

    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Port Alberni pricing depends on size and weight. Standard courier to oversized freight—we handle it all.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border border-gray-300 mb-6 space-y-4">
        <div class="pb-4 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Standard Delivery (Small Package)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">$35 base + (80 km × $2.00) = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$195</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Standard courier, documents, small parts. Example: Engineering drawings, lab samples.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-4 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Freight / Oversized (Van)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">$50 base + (80 km × $2.50) + weight surcharge = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$280–$350</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Equipment parts, machinery, forest products up to 1 pallet. Example: Mill parts, manufacturing supplies.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-4 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Box Truck (Large Freight)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">$75 base + (80 km × $3.00) + weight surcharge = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$400–$550</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Multi-pallet loads, pulp & paper supplies, bulk materials. Example: Production line restocking.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Rush Multiplier (After 1 PM)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Standard rate × 1.5 = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$290–$825 depending on size</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Emergency equipment failure. Drivers prioritized; mountain route risk managed with chains/experience.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
        High-volume Port Alberni account? Weekly freight routes available. Pulp/paper mills often contract monthly. Call for volume pricing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Port Alberni Route FAQ</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Do you handle heavy industrial freight?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. Box truck option available for multi-pallet loads. We work with mills, pulp plants, and manufacturing. Weight limits apply; quote based on weight + dimensions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">What's your experience with forestry/lumber products?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Extensive. Port Alberni's main industry. We've handled equipment parts, finished lumber, forestry supplies, mill components. Safe handling of heavy/bulky items guaranteed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Winter cutoff: Do I need to order earlier?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. Summer (May–Oct): 1 PM cutoff. Winter (Nov–Mar): 11 AM cutoff for same-day guarantee. Mountain passes add time. We monitor roads; if bad, we'll call you with revised timing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Can you handle return shipments (defects back to Nanaimo)?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. Pickup in Port Alberni, delivery to Nanaimo supplier. Same pricing structure. Useful for logistics loops: new parts out, defects back.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Do you offer standing weekly/monthly freight contracts?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. Mills and manufacturers often need predictable weekly routes. We can optimize cost with fixed monthly rates. Call to discuss your volume.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteForm />
</BaseLayout>
